      "featured": true,
      "notes_md": "- **Why:** it prefills about 23% faster than `vllm-8a72` (P6 4k median 2,163 vs 1,756 tok/s on the same-day control) and cuts long-image TTFT about 15%, with no detectable change in single-stream decode, accept length or graded answers.\n- **What the fork carries on v0.30.0:** the disk-backed PLE staged gather (dtype-aware: FP8 + global scale for the NVIDIA checkpoint, BF16 without a scale for Swift), the reduced-vocab 65,536 MTP draft head, and cherry-picks of vllm#55557 (fp8 KV on QSA), #57105 (QSA indexer logits workspace) and #58961 (frees the profiling KV held by QSA key views). The FP8 scale is verified once after the whole weight stream, logged as `PLE disk: post-load verify OK`.\n- **Measured (2026-09-30/10-01):** weights 76.5 GiB loaded in ~600 s, ready ~11 min after the request; the KV pool varies about 12% between boots of the same image and flags (569,302, 540,175 and 603,725 tokens); MemAvailable at ready 19.2 GiB, lowest 9.8 GiB during a 100-frame request. `max-num-batched-tokens=8192` was tested and rejected.\n- **Verified:** `behavior_check.sh` ok both cases; 100-frame and 120-frame image requests return valid JSON.\n- **Rollback:** set `image:` to `vllm-flash-next:8a728663-baked-v1` and the cache mount to `/opt/ai/cache/vllm-flash-next` in `serve/compose.flash-next-vllm.yaml`. The rollback image and cache are untouched."
